# Privacy Policy for تذكّر | Remember

Effective date: 2026-10-19

Developer: Ramy Khashan  
Privacy/support contact: ramykhashan99@gmail.com

This policy describes the current intended data practices of تذكّر | Remember, an app for creating notes, organizing tasks and reminders, and recording voice notes. The app does not require an account.

## Information Handled On Your Device

The app lets you enter note and task content, choose photos to attach to notes, and make voice recordings. It also stores app settings such as language and theme. The inspected app code stores this content in a local database or app-private files to provide the app's features. The inspected Dart code does not send this content to a developer-operated server. This statement must be checked against all bundled SDKs and the final release build before publication.

## Permissions

The microphone is used when you choose to record a voice note. Photo access is used when you choose photos to attach to a note. Notification and alarm-related permissions are used for task reminders. You can manage permissions in your device settings; denying permission may disable the related feature.

## Sharing And Third Parties

The current source review found no account system, advertising, analytics, or developer-operated backend. The developer must verify this against all third-party SDKs included in the release build. Android system backup and restore may handle app data according to device and account settings. The developer must verify the app's backup behavior and update this section before publication.

## Retention And Deletion

Content remains in the app's local storage until you delete it or remove the app. You can delete notes, tasks, and voice notes from within the app. If device backups are enabled, backup copies may remain under the device account's backup controls after local deletion. Verify this behavior for the release build.

## Security

The app stores local content in app storage managed by Android. The inspected code does not provide app-level encryption for the local database or recordings. Use your device's screen lock and backup controls to protect access to your information.

## Children

The developer indicates that the app's intended audience includes ages 6-8, 9-12, and 13+. The app, its content, permissions, and every included SDK must comply with Google Play's Families policy and applicable child-privacy laws before publishing.

## Changes To This Policy

If the app's data practices change, this policy will be updated and the effective date above will change.

## Contact

For privacy questions, contact ramykhashan99@gmail.com.

